      <transcript>SINEDKE-</transcript>
      <definition>[v. caus. of sined-] v. t. To renew, renovate; reform, reconstruct, reorganize.</definition>
      <page>711</page>
      <examples>
        <example>
          <unicode> ᠰᠢᠨᠡᠳᠬᠡᠭᠰᠡᠨ ᠱᠠᠰᠢᠨ</unicode>
          <transcript>--gsen šasin</transcript>
          <definition> Reformed religion.</definition>
        </example>
        <example>
          <unicode> ᠰᠢᠨᠡᠳᠬᠡᠨ ᠪᠠᠶᠢᠭᠤᠯᠬᠤ</unicode>
          <transcript>-—n baiγulxu </transcript>
          <definition>To reconstruct, reorganize, rebuild, reform</definition>
        </example>
        <example>
          <unicode> ᠰᠢᠨᠡᠳᠬᠡ ᠰᠠᠶᠢᠵᠢᠷᠠᠭᠤᠯᠬᠤ</unicode>
          <transcript>--n saiziraγulxu</transcript>
          <definition> To improve, reform</definition>
        </example>
        <example>
          <unicode> ᠰᠢᠨᠡᠳᠬᠡᠨ ᠵᠠᠰᠠᠭᠤᠯᠬᠤ</unicode>
